media: i2c: hi847: add device tree support with regulators, reset and MCLK

The mainline Hi847 driver is ACPI-only and lets ACPI power resources
handle the sensor's rails, clock and reset. On the Galaxy Tab S8+ the
Hi847 is the rear ultrawide sensor on CCI0 (7-bit 0x21) with externally
switched LDOs, a reset line and MCLK1 from camcc, so it needs the same
OF plumbing hi846.c has: compatible hynix,hi847, vddio/vdda/vddd
regulators, optional reset-gpios and shutdown-gpios, and runtime PM
power on/off around the clock.

Power-up follows the stock CamX sequence for this module: rails on,
5 ms, MCLK on at 19.2 MHz, 8 ms, reset released, 11 ms. Power-down
reverses it. With no GPIOs and dummy regulators the ACPI path behaves
as before. The clock helper does not set a rate on DT, so probe sets
19.2 MHz and fails if the clock cannot deliver it.

Binding Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/hynix,hi847.yaml
follows hynix,hi846.yaml with four data lanes. The driver's hardware
check requires both 400 MHz and 200 MHz in link-frequencies.

Register tables are untouched. Comparison against the stock module's
CamX tables is recorded in issue #27 (stage 2 comment).

